  "assessor": "writer self-assessment; independent integrator review pending",
  "notes": "The feature is a behavior change (new clamping bounds) to the existing Device Memory API, not new API surface. The inventory therefore covers the migration itself, the value-computation algorithm whose bounds changed, and the three developer-facing surfaces the change affects (navigator.deviceMemory on Window+Worker, Sec-CH-Device-Memory, and the legacy Device-Memory header). The base API's full reference is owned by MDN (linked in see-also); this page documents the change and enough of each affected contract to act on it. All items are documented on the overview page: no member is a new contract needing a child route.",
